"The postoperative pathology reveals a Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2) diagnosis with pathological stage pT3a and positive surgical margins. A reassuring finding is that the seminal vesicles were not invaded, and lymphovascular invasion was absent. The status of the lymph nodes is not documented, and the report indicates \"no lymph nodes were removed.\" The preoperative PSA was 5.4. The positive margins and T3a extension are adverse prognostic factors. Countervailing findings include the absence of seminal vesicle invasion and lymphovascular invasion. The lack of documented nodal sampling widens the uncertainty regarding regional disease control, as \"No nodes sampled; pNx is not pN0.\" Postoperative PSA is not recorded, meaning biochemical recurrence cannot be assessed. Information regarding postoperative PSA and its trajectory is crucial for revising the prognosis. The fixed estimated horizon is 64.83 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 38.90–90.77 months; its coverage has not been validated."
